  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0014 database is used to manage a community platform, storing information about users, discussions, posts, and various other entities. The database consists of 24 tables, each representing a specific entity or relationship within the platform. The users table stores information about individual users, including their username, email, password, and preferences. Each user can have multiple access tokens, which are used for authentication and authorization, and are linked to the user's ID through a foreign key. Users can also have multiple login providers, which allow them to log in using external services such as social media or email. The users table is referenced by several other tables, including the discussions, posts, and notifications tables, which store information about discussions, posts, and notifications sent to users. Discussions are represented by the discussions table, which stores information about the discussion title, comment count, and participant count, as well as the ID of the user who created the discussion. Each discussion can have multiple posts, which are stored in the posts table, and each post is linked to the discussion ID through a foreign key. Posts can also have multiple likes, which are stored in the post_likes table, and can be mentioned in other posts, which are stored in the post_mentions_post table. Users can also be mentioned in posts, which are stored in the post_mentions_user table. The tags table stores information about tags, which can be applied to discussions and posts, and the tag_user table stores information about which users have applied which tags to their discussions and posts. The groups table stores information about groups, which can be created by users and have their own permissions, and the group_permission table stores information about which permissions are assigned to which groups. The password_tokens, email_tokens, and registration_tokens tables store information about tokens used for password recovery, email verification, and registration, respectively. The flags table stores information about flags raised on posts, and the notifications table stores information about notifications sent to users. The settings table stores information about the platform's settings, and the migrations table stores information about database migrations.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nFlarum is a simple yet powerful discussion platform designed to facilitate community engagement and interaction. It caters to a wide range of community sizes, from small groups to enterprise-level organizations. Built on a core framework, Flarum is highly extensible and offers extensive customization options through various extensions.\n\n 2) Objectives\n\n- Develop a discussion platform that supports community interaction.\n- Provide extensibility and customization to meet diverse community needs.\n- Ensure scalable performance regardless of community size.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Community Members: Users who participate in discussions.\n- Administrators: Users who manage and customize the forum.\n- Developers: Individuals or teams extending/customizing the platform.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- User Registration: Users can create accounts to participate in discussions.\n- Permission Management: Configurable permission groups for access control and defining actions like moderation.\n- Discussion and Post Management: Users can create, comment, and manage discussions and posts.\n- Content Editing: Support for simple editors like bbcode/markdown and WYSIWYG for creating posts.\n- Theme and Style Customization: Administrators can customize appearance via themes and custom CSS.\n- Real-time Interaction: Notifications and updates through in-browser and email communication. Option for websocket integration for real-time updates.\n- Extension Support: Facility to extend functionality through numerous available extensions or custom development.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Capable of supporting communities of varying sizes efficiently.\n- Extensibility: Hundreds of extensions available with options for further customization.\n- Usability: Intuitive interface for both community members and administrators.\n- Security: Secure handling of user data and transactions, with features like tokenized access and API key management.\n- Performance: Optimized to ensure quick response times and fluid user experience even under heavy load.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0014.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0014\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `preferences` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `access_tokens` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `access_tokens_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `login_providers` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `provider` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `login_providers_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `discussions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `participant_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `discussions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `posts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `discussion_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`discussion_id`) REFERENCES `discussions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `post_likes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `post_likes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `post_likes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `post_mentions_post` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `mentioned_post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `post_mentions_post_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `post_mentions_post_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`mentioned_post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `post_mentions_user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `mentioned_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `post_mentions_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `post_mentions_user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`mentioned_user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tag_user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tag_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tag_user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`tag_id`) REFERENCES `tags` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `groups` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_by` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `groups_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`created_by`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `group_permission` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `group_permission_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `groups` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `password_tokens` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `password_tokens_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `email_tokens` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `email_tokens_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `registration_tokens` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `registration_tokens_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `flags` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reason` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notifications` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notifications_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `settings` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `value` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `migrations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `version` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
